Spec folder: specs/cli-external-orchestration/082-opencode-v1-v2-dual-compat/040-dispatch-lint-held-fixes (pre-approved, skip Gate 3)

ROLE: Act as a code agent. Make one change: widen how `isUsableMention` in `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts` reads a refusal of the executor, plus test rows. The guiding rule: when a phrasing cannot be read safely as a request, the mention does NOT authorize (fail closed).

Current behaviour: the sentence starts after newline/;/./!/? or a contrast word (but, instead, rather); `negationReachesMention` finds the last `NEGATION_PATTERN` match and lets a comma end it when an executor is named between the negation and the comma and an imperative (use, run, ...) follows the comma.

Changes:
1. Curly apostrophes: at the start of `isUsableMention`, read a normalized copy of the text in which `’` and `‘` are replaced by `'` (same length, so indexes hold), and use it for every check below and for the existing contraction handling.
2. `NEGATION_PATTERN` also matches, as whole words, case-insensitive: `cannot`, `can't`, `can not`, `mustn't`, `must not`, `shouldn't`, `should not`, `won't`, `will not`, `no`, `nor`, `neither`. Keep the existing words.
3. Lists: in `negationReachesMention`, a comma may end the negation only when, in addition to the two existing conditions, the text from just after that comma to the mention contains no further comma and no whole word `and` or `or`. So `do not use opencode, use codex, or use cli-devin` stays negated, while `not opencode, use cli-devin` still ends it.
4. Exclusion phrases right before the mention: before applying the contrast-word sentence start, if the text before the mention, with trailing spaces removed, ends with one of these whole phrases (case-insensitive), the mention is negated: `instead of`, `rather than`, `except`, `except for`, `other than`, `apart from`, `aside from`, `besides`, `excluding`, `anything but`, `everything but`, `all but`, `but not`, `not even`, `no`, `without`.
5. Refusals after the mention: take the text from the end of the mention's token (the run of non-space characters starting at the mention index; for a `/deep:` mention, continue to the end of its `--executor cli-X` value) to the next newline, `;`, `.`, `!` or `?`. The mention is negated if that text contains, as whole words or phrases (case-insensitive): `forbidden`, `banned`, `disallowed`, `prohibited`, `off-limits`, `off limits`, `not allowed`, `not permitted`, `is not`, `isn't`, `are not`, `aren't`, `must not`, `mustn't`, `should not`, `shouldn't`, `cannot`, `can't`, `can not`, `won't`, `will not`. A plain `, not opencode` after the mention does not count.
Keep the quote and expansion checks. Put each new word list in a named constant beside `NEGATION_PATTERN`, and update the function comments so they stay accurate and short.

